# Identity-check allowlist — see .github/scripts/check-persona-names.py
#
# EMPTY BY DESIGN, AND IT SHOULD STAY THAT WAY.
#
# A finding from this check is almost always a defect in the publish-side
# rename rules, and the fix belongs there. An entry here fixes the symptom in
# one place and leaves the mechanism free to re-introduce the same leak in the
# next file it touches. Prefer fixing the rename; reach for this only when the
# occurrence is genuinely intentional and cannot be expressed as a rule.
#
# Note that the two intentional-attribution cases are ALREADY handled by the
# check itself and need no entry here:
#   * the Licensor's personal name in LICENSE / NOTICE / COMMERCIAL.md /
#     pyproject.toml authors;
#   * the public GitHub handle in URL or owner/repo slug form.
#
# Entry forms:
#   <path>:<lineno>   exempt that one line's content
#   <path>:*          exempt that file's content entirely
#   path=<path>       exempt that file's PATH from the path scan
#
# One entry per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
